    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0569" n="559" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg559"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 31.</seg></opener>
                <head>Lord Lyons to Earl
                        Russell.—(Received March 17.)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> With reference to my despatch of the
                    29th ultimo, I have the honor to inclose a copy of a note from Mr. Seward
                    acknowledging with satisfaction <pb facs="0570" n="560" xml:id="pg560"/> the
                    receipt of the note dated the 29th ultimo, in which I informed him that her
                    Majesty’s government accepted the apology offered by the government of the
                    United States for the violation of British territory committed by its officers
                    in the case of the Chesapeake.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d294-a1.xml" xpointer="d294-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
